// The positive control for the method route: `caller` holds `process` (with no
// program at all, which is what `Child`'s own methods need) and calls two of
// them. The domain gate admits the names and no resource pattern is consulted,
// because a method names no resource the grant governs.
impl "caller" caps(process = [])

fun main() {
    print(caller.probe())
}
